# Realm powers — discovering what a power opens, land by land
# A design, proposed. Mechanics only. Nothing here is built; the powers named as kept are already in the lanes
# (book/scripts/home/pie-powers.mjs POWER_SPELLS), and the forms named as proposed are not.
#>lore_land_surfaces_realm_powers
#:surface #!proposal
#:operation #!prime
#:fixity #!experimental
#:layer #!pragmatics

~<rationale>{
  The best moment with a power is not getting it. It is going back to a room you already passed and finding that the power has changed what the room is. A wall you walked round becomes a wall you fit under. A beam you went round becomes a beam you stand on. So powers here are kept per land, each land keeping the kind of power its question asks for, and each one is shown first as a change in how you move, never as a number. A room only hints at what a power would open after you have held that power once, so nothing is teased that cannot yet be had. A few rooms have a second way out, found only with the right power, and it leads somewhere the main way does not.
}

^"each_land_keeps"{
  boon: "powers of seeing ahead and of being small enough: possibility, a way before it is needed, a gap only a little thing fits"
  bane: "powers of weight and contract: you are bound to the pie and nothing tips you, but you cannot hop, and what you walk through breaks, and is remembered"
  bone: "powers of structure: what holds you up becomes somewhere to stand, and the load is shown"
}

^"kept_powers_by_land"{
  .note: "every power already in the lanes, sorted by the land whose question it answers"
  boon: "boonberry ~glimpse (the clear way, a breath early) · echo_wrens *echoes · jazz_geese !honk · page_fox ~unkept and !ready · hob_deer ~unkept (a deer no taller than a boot)"
  bane: "frill_lichen *frill (knocks land on the ruffle, at a price of edge) · sliver_tin *tin (always filling, never full) · remainder_moths ~true_aim · lag_stag ~lag (the land lands a beat late, on credit)"
  bone: "boneberry ~fed · pane_snails !level and &without[pane] (the glass forgiven) · salt_whales ~lit (the old roads under the crust) · beaver ~lag (its own time, lent) · torch_ants ~lit (the streets kept lit)"
}

^"proposed_forms"{
  small: "*seedling{ ~small[6] } (boon). The carrier is the size of a boonberry for a while: a mime's invisible wall stops at your knee, so you pass under it, and the gap in a march is wide enough. Slices are smaller too, so a clown wants two. Found where the hob-deer is, and first used on a wall you have already gone round"
  bound: "*clause{ ~bound[6] } (bane). The carrier signs for the pie: knocks do not tilt it, hops are not allowed, and posts and panes in your lane break as you pass. Nothing happens at once when glass breaks; the mimes remember it. Found in a chapter that leans bane, and priced in the open before it is taken"
  frame: "*joist{ ~frame[6] } (bone). The carrier can stand on what others go round: the dividers become a beam to walk, and a raised row of the lane, seen and never reachable, can be reached. The heights panel shows the load. Found where the frame is tapped and answers"
}

^"discovery"[
  { step: "a power changes how you move, shown once, in a room that suits it" }
  { step: "back in a chapter you carried before, a room is marked with what the power would open, but only once you have held it" }
  { step: "a few rooms keep a second way out: cast the room with the right land's power and the carry leaves by it, to a chapter out of order, a piece of texture.website, or an event route" }
  { step: "each land's powers are found in the chapters that lean its way, so the book read by lean is the map of the realms" }
  { step: "a land's last gate wants its three marks, one per kind of room, and gives nothing but the way through" }
]

!guards[
  "A power changes how you move or what you can reach. A bigger number on its own is not a power here"
  "No room hints at what it hides before the power has been held once"
  "Every bane power is priced in the open before it is taken, and its cost comes later, never as a punishment the player did not see priced"
  "A second way out never skips story a reader has not read; it goes sideways, not ahead"
]

?open[
  "Are the forms new kinds in the almanac, or gifts of wonders already there (the hob-deer for small, the frame-tapping for joist)"
  "Does breaking glass while bound feed the mimes memory (the main session is building mimes who remember a shattered pane), or is that only for thrown slices"
  "Which rooms keep a second way out, and where does each lead"
  "Is the last gate per land a room, a chapter, or a card"
]
